# evaluation.fixtures — the fixtures both test suites run.
#
# X1.3 EXISTS TO STOP A SECOND IMPLEMENTATION GROWING IN C#, and the only way to catch that is to
# put the same problem through both paths and compare the numbers. So the fixtures live here,
# owned by neither side: tests/native/test_fixtures.cpp reads this file and checks the ENGINE
# against the recorded values; ThinFilm.Native.Tests reads the same file and checks DESIGN against
# them. Neither suite can quietly drift onto a fixture of its own.
#
# WHERE THE EXPECTED NUMBERS COME FROM. They were produced by the engine and recorded here
# (test_fixtures --regenerate). That is legitimate precisely because the engine is already checked
# against physics elsewhere — 1750 native checks including Fresnel, quarter-wave, half-wave
# absentee, energy conservation and analytic-vs-finite-difference derivatives. This file is not
# where the engine is proved right; it is where the two CALLERS are proved to agree with it. If
# the engine changes, the native suite fails first and says so; if only the managed side fails,
# the fault is in the binding and nowhere else. The separation of blame is the point.
#
# FORMAT, deliberately dull so that both parsers are twenty lines and neither can be interesting:
#
#   fixture <name>            begins one
#   i <key> <int> ...         an int array (a scalar is an array of one)
#   d <key> <double> ...      a double array, written %.17g so it round-trips exactly
#   c <key> <re> <im> ...     a complex array, interleaved
#   end                       ends it
#
# Keys are the ABI's own field names. Counts are not stated: n_layers is the length of
# layer_thickness, n_points of point_angle, n_operands of code, and so on.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A bare substrate. The one case whose answer can be checked by hand: R = ((1-1.52)/(1+1.52))^2.
fixture bare_substrate
i n_materials 1
c material_index 1.46 0
d wavelength 550
i point_wavelength 0
d point_angle 0
c index_incident 1 0
c index_exit 1.52 0
i code 0
i point 0
d target 0
d weight 1
d expect_value 0.042579994960947345
d expect_residual 0.042579994960947345
d expect_merit 0.042579994960947345
end

